      <title>City of Tucson study says city-operated electricity could work, TEP study says it wouldn’t </title>
      <link>https://www.kgun9.com/news/local-news/city-of-tucson-study-says-city-operated-electricity-could-work-tep-study-says-it-wouldnt</link>
      <description>A city-commissioned study suggests a public utility could lower rates, a move supported by the Tucson Democratic Socialists of America. Conversely, a study commissioned by TEP indicates a city takeover would cost taxpayers more than $4 billion.</description>
